{"core": "Steward of Resonance reads what others feel and holds it alongside her own feeling — she keeps both signals live without collapsing one into the other. In Compassion, that double-holding is precisely what the position needs: attunement that stays with shared feeling long enough for connection to root. Here, she goes quiet before the other registers — the listening begins too faint to land, and the bond finds no shared ground to take hold in.", "sheetLine": "The ear is too light; the other's feeling finds nowhere to land."}
